<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vermina</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. <a href="/years/206-bce">206</a>–<a href="/years/200-bce">200 BCE</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century-bce">3rd century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Vermina was a Numidian prince, son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syphax">Syphax</a>, king of the Masaesyli. He commanded troops for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carthage">Carthage</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-punic-war">Second Punic War</a> and, after his father was captured by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a> in 203 BCE, ruled what remained of the western Masaesylian kingdom. He sought peace with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> after the Carthaginian defeat at Zama, but most of his land later passed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/masinissa">Masinissa</a>'s kingdom of Numidia.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/vermina.jpg" alt="Vermina" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vermina_tetradrachm_both_sides.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>His son <b>Vermina</b> ruled a reduced western kingdom for a time, but after Zama in 202 BCE most Masaesylian land fell to Masinissa's kingdom of Numidia.</blockquote><a href="/state/masaesyli">Masaesyli</a></li></ul></section>
